    "title": "fix(characters): separate Traveler ascension materials from talent materials, and sync ascension state across all 7 elements",
    "body": "Traveler ascension (level, gems, EXP books, ascension Mora) is one\nshared progression in-game regardless of which element is active, but\ntalent materials are genuinely independent per element. Previously\nthis app treated both as fully independent across all 7 Traveler\nrows, which let rows disagree on level/ascension and multiplied\nascension material totals by 7x in roster-wide sums.\n\n- traveler.json: added ascension_enemy_material_family_id (Hilichurl\n  Mask series) as a dedicated field for ascension calculations, kept\n  separate from the existing enemy_material_family_id used for talent\n  materials, so fixing one no longer accidentally changes the other\n- useStore.js: editing level/ascension/target-level/target-ascension\n  on any tracked Traveler row now propagates the same values to every\n  other tracked Traveler row, across all update paths (character\n  modal, bulk edit, batch add) — talent fields remain fully\n  independent per element, unchanged\n- aggregator.js: roster-wide totals (My Roster, Dashboard, Planner)\n  now count ascension materials once across all tracked Traveler\n  elements combined instead of summing per-row; talent materials\n  continue to be summed per element as before\n- dataManager.js/resolver.js: Traveler-family detection used by the\n  above sync and aggregation logic\n\nIndividual per-character material views (config modal, Planner's\nper-character tab) are unaffected — each row still shows its own full\nascension + talent requirements.",
