    "title": "feat(weapons): add weapon crafting/forging system",
    "body": "Adds forging/crafting material tracking for craftable weapons, replacing\nthe standalone craft-queue with inline refinement tracking on the\nexisting My Armory table.\n\n- src/data/weapon_forging.json: recipes (billet + ores + mora) for all\n  43 currently craftable weapons, including Nod-Krai and Snezhnaya\n- src/data/crafting_materials.json: flat inventory-trackable list of all\n  billets and forging ores referenced across recipes\n- My Armory table: current/target Refinement columns (R0 = not owned,\n  R1-R5 = owned copies), inline-editable like existing Lv columns;\n  disabled for non-craftable weapons\n- My Armory table: new \"Forging\" column group (Billet | Regional Ore |\n  Common Ore | Mora) showing per-row and totaled forging cost for any\n  weapon with a refinement delta\n- Add/Edit Weapon modal: \"Planning to craft\" toggle for weapons not yet\n  owned — locks current state to 0, target state stays editable so\n  forging + ascension needs can be planned before the weapon is crafted\n- Inventory: new \"Crafting Mats\" tab (Billet / Forging Ore sub-tabs)\n- Planner: new \"Crafting Materials\" tab, Need/Have/To Farm per material,\n  merged into existing inventory-subtracted totals\n- Icon resolution for all of the above routed through the existing\n  getMaterialIcon() resolver (crafting_materials/ CDN folder) instead of\n  per-surface hardcoded paths\n\nRemoves the earlier standalone craftQueue store slice — refinement\ndeltas on trackedWeapons entries now serve as the single source of\ntruth for both display and cost aggregation.",
    "type": "added",
    "url": "https://github.com/ItsCryp7iC/travelers-toolkit/commit/61628e9dffd6545009fd45c1652f519ba3829f7c"
